cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "VaultKG: Obsidian Vaults as Knowledge Graphs"
abstract: >
  VaultKG turns an Obsidian-style Markdown vault into a queryable knowledge
  graph. Notes, headings, tags, attachments and unresolved link targets are
  nodes; wikilinks, Markdown links, embeds, tags and typed links (Dataview
  inline fields and frontmatter keys holding wikilinks) are edges. The graph
  is parsed from what the author wrote, with no model extraction, so the same
  vault always builds the same graph. It supports semantic search with link
  expansion, backlinks, a graph-health report and metric snapshots, through a
  CLI and an MCP server.
